Chapter: LinLaunderLocalDup
  cites Foreword chapter Linear

 Probe (closed by LinearOwnership stage 2): aliasing the linear
 param to a let-local is a MOVE; the local inherits the exactly-once
 obligation. Using the local twice is a double-spend - CDX2061.

Section: Definitions

  dup : linear Integer -> Integer
  dup (n) = let h = n
   in h + h

  opening : Text = show (dup 21)

